WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome, everybody. Welcome.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:07.968
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."
What a show we have for you.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.300
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.767
Tom Hiddleston and Brie Larson
are my guests tonight.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:14.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:18.634
That's right. Loki and
Captain Marvel are here.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.767
I got to say,
going to Comic-Con is fun,

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.567
but it's even more fun
when it comes to you.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.968
You know what I'm saying?
Come on.

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.934
That's right.
Loki is here tonight.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:33.434
And speaking of
the God of Mischief,

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:37.133
former President Trump
is in the news.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:40.434
That's right, Trump's classified
documents trial is coming up,

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:43.033
and I read that prosecutors
may call for testimony

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:44.467
from workers at Mar-a-Lago,

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:48.734
including a plumber, a maid,
a chauffeur and a woodworker.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.701
So clearly, Trump hid his
documents in the toilet,

00:00:53.701 --> 00:01:00.367
the closet, the car,
and Eric and Don Jr's treehouse.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.701
That's right, a plumber, a maid,
a chauffeur, and a woodworker

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.934
could be called
to testify against Trump.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:07.133
And we actually got our hands
on the plumber's interview

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.167
with the lawyers.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.968
-Really?
-Yeah, listen to this.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.501
[ Crowd groans ]
-Oh, hey.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.567
-What?
-What is...?

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:46.133
-Why would he ask that?

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.834
-Why?
-That seems ridiculous.

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.834
I don't know why he asked.
It seems what?

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:52.634
-Ri-dic-ulous.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:56.434
[ Rim shot ]

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.834
-Well, changing subjects --
people are talking about this.

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:02.234
New York City Mayor Eric Adams
is under investigation

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.834
for receiving
illegal campaign donations,

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:08.234
and apparently,
the FBI just seized his phones.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.434
Yeah.

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.567
Everyone was like,
"Phones? Plural?

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.934
Oh, yeah. He's guilty."

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.901
Yeah, phones?

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.234
When New Yorkers heard
about the news about the mayor,

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:20.067
just out of habit, they were
like, "friggin' de Blasio."

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.300
What?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.300
Hey, guys, this is exciting.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.367
The 2024 Grammy nominations
were announced today.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:37.467
And some of the top nominees,
including SZA,

00:02:37.467 --> 00:02:40.300
the "Barbie" soundtrack,
and Taylor Swift.

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:45.567
Taylor has
a bunch of nominations.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.834
Let's just say that she could
become the first artist

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:51.534
to break 10,000 steps
at an award show.

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:53.167
It's crazy,
this year, Taylor Swift

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:57.801
could win a Grammy,
an Oscar, and the NFL MVP.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:03:01.367
All three.
No one's ever done it.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:03.434
Speaking of Taylor,
a man in Maryland

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.501
started a Taylor Swift jar

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.100
that his wife had to put
a dollar into

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.534
every time
she mentions Taylor Swift.

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.701
Well, it turns out
a lot of people have jars

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:14.534
to get them to stop
doing certain things.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.133
I'll show you what I mean in
a new segment called

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.434
Other Jars.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:19.501
-♪ Other jars, other jars ♪

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:22.968
♪ Now it's time
for other jars ♪

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.968
-First up, Mitch McConnell
has to put a dollar in his jar

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.200
every time he starts buffering.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.300
-♪ Other jars ♪

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.100
-Next up, Chip and Joanna Gaines

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.601
have to put a dollar
in their jar

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:37.634
every time they say
the word "shiplap."

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:38.801
-♪ That's another jar ♪

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.400
-Here's the next one.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.400
Joe Biden has to put
a dollar in his jar

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.767
every time he calls
a 70-year-old "kiddo."

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:47.200
-♪ I call that another jar ♪

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.000
-Yeah, and finally,
here's the last one,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.133
Gerry, the Golden Bachelor,
has to put a dollar in his jar

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:57.300
every time he makes you ugly cry
by just being himself.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.234
That's it for "Other Jars."

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:06.267
No. That's all.
That was the last one.

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:10.734
-♪ Come on, man,
just one more jar ♪

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.367
-Uh, okay. Here's one.

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:14.901
Ron DeSantis has to put
a dollar in his jar

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.734
every time he stands
on his tippy toes

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:19.601
to see the options at Chipotle.

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.434
-♪ One more jar ♪

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:23.167
-No, another?

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.834
I really don't have any more.
There's no more jars.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.701
-♪ One more jar ♪

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:30.767
-No more jars.
-♪ One more jar ♪

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:33.067
-No more jars.
-♪ One more jar ♪

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:34.834
-The bit is over. I'm sorry.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.133
-[ Deep, rattling voice ]
♪ You must give me ♪

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.534
♪ One more jar ♪

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:38.801
♪ I am all powerful ♪

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:43.067
♪ Deliverest me thou jar
or perish! ♪

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:45.200
-Alright, alright.
Okay, okay. Uh...

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.067
Donald Trump has to put
a dollar in his jar

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:49.901
every time he shows up to court
and asks to meet Judge Judy.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:52.234
-♪ That is all for Other Jars ♪

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:54.434
-Whew.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:57.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.467
-And finally, everybody,
the Census Bureau just announced

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:06.033
that the world population
has topped 8 billion.

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:07.334
So on behalf of everyone,

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.534
I just want to say
thank you to Nick Cannon.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:10.801
We have a great show tonight.

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:14.033
-Give it up for The Roots!
Come on!

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.434
[ Cheering ]

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.767
♪ Dogs at my doorstep
will come around ♪

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.234
♪ Go around like the vortex ♪

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:23.067
♪ Competition, I'm all for it,
quartet ♪

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:25.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:27.067
-Hey, everybody.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:28.601
As I said, Grammy nominations

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:31.067
came out today,
just this afternoon.

00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:32.534
And I want
to say congratulations

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.467
to our very own Tariq Trotter,

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.167
who got nominated for a Grammy!

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:40.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:42.734
Yes!

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:45.901
-Tariq got nominated
for Best Rap Performance

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:46.801
for your song "Love Letter."

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.267
Congratulations, buddy.

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:49.767
Come on. Black Thought!

00:05:49.767 --> 00:05:51.734
Black Thought, right there!
Come on!

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:55.534
Congratulations.
That's how you do it.

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:57.300
That made me happy. Come on.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.934
I also want to mention,
all next week,

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:01.667
you're going to see
how I arrive to work every day,

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.167
when I walk in the building.
-Really?

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:05.234
-It's a new thing, like they do
with the NBA players

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:06.300
in the arena?
-Right.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.801
-Yeah, it's very similar to me,

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:09.100
right down
to some of my outfits.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.834
Anyway, it's going to be
"Tonight Show" Entrance Week.

00:06:11.834 --> 00:06:12.868
-Ooh, wow.

00:06:12.868 --> 00:06:14.968
-So tune in for that.
-The whole week?

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:16.133
-Yeah, the whole week.

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:17.467
But first, what a show
we have for you tonight.

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:19.934
He is an Emmy
and Tony-nominated actor

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:23.300
whose series "Loki" is now
streaming its second season

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.634
on Disney Plus.

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:27.000
Tom Hiddleston is here!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:38.200
Plus, she's an Oscar winner
who you can see in the Apple TV+

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.434
series "Lessons in Chemistry,"
and her new film

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:44.601
"The Marvels"
opened in theaters today.

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:48.033
Brie Larson is joining us.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:51.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:54.801
-Plus, he is a comedy legend,

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:58.000
one of my favorite
comedians ever.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.868
He wrote the musical "Spamalot,"

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:02.868
which is back on Broadway
at the Saint James Theater.

00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:05.334
Eric Idle is here,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:08.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:12.634
And we got great music tonight,
Rick Ross and Meek Mill.

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:14.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:20.200
Guys, today is Friday,
and that's usually

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.667
when we catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:23.567
I check my inbox,
return some emails,

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:25.367
and of course
I send out thank you notes.

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:27.267
And I was running a bit behind.
Is that okay?

00:07:27.267 --> 00:07:29.501
Can I write out
some thank you notes now?

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:30.601
I appreciate that.

00:07:30.601 --> 00:07:31.734
James, can I get some

00:07:31.734 --> 00:07:33.367
thank you note-writing music,
please?

00:07:33.367 --> 00:07:35.934
[ Gentle music playing ]

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:41.834
♪♪

00:07:41.834 --> 00:07:43.501
Thank you, Ohio,

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.901
for legalizing
recreational weed.

00:07:45.901 --> 00:07:48.400
[ Cheering ]

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.267
Wait, you're telling me
a state known for eating chili

00:07:51.267 --> 00:07:55.801
on top of spaghetti just now
legalized weed?

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:57.767
-Come on, Ohio.

00:08:01.133 --> 00:08:02.400
-Thank you,

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:05.300
the "Golden Bachelor"'s
Women Tell All episode

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.634
for starting with a warning

00:08:06.634 --> 00:08:10.200
that the show may be disturbing
to viewers under 65.

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:20.601
Thank you, Election Day,
for forcing all of us

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:22.667
to make exceptionally
important decisions

00:08:22.667 --> 00:08:25.133
in our old high school
gymnasium.

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:32.300
Thank you,

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.601
apartment smoke detector,
for alerting me

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:37.868
there's a fire by doing
a Mariah Carey impression.

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.534
Thank you, autocorrect,

00:08:47.534 --> 00:08:49.934
for waiting until
the exact second I hit "send"

00:08:49.934 --> 00:08:51.667
to ruin a message.

00:08:59.334 --> 00:09:00.868
Thank you,

00:09:00.868 --> 00:09:05.033
Pizza Hut Hong Kong's
new snake pizza

00:09:05.033 --> 00:09:06.701
for being the first time
a delivery guy says,

00:09:06.701 --> 00:09:07.901
"Who ordered the snake pizza?"

00:09:07.901 --> 00:09:09.734
and it's not
the start of a porno.

00:09:09.734 --> 00:09:11.067
You guys, we --

00:09:11.067 --> 00:09:12.367
There you have it.
Those are our thank you notes.

00:09:12.367 --> 00:09:14.968
We'll be right back with
Tom Hiddleston, everybody!

